#. Keep our friendship close. It has served us both, and it shall serve one of us again.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/backstabber/0"
msgstr "Tenons notre amitié pour chose précieuse. Elle nous a servis tous deux, et servira derechef l'un de nous."

#. There is no quarrel between us — yet. Consider how rare that is in these waters.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/backstabber/1"
msgstr "Il n'y a nulle querelle entre nous — pas encore. Songez combien cela est rare en ces eaux."

#. Do not mistake a warm letter for a warm intention. We write to several courts.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/backstabber/2"
msgstr "Ne prenez pas une lettre chaleureuse pour une intention chaude. Nous écrivons à plusieurs cours."

#. Your new buildings are fine work. Ours shall be finer, and sooner than you think.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/envy/0"
msgstr "Vos nouveaux bâtiments sont bel ouvrage. Les nôtres seront plus beaux, et plus tôt que vous ne pensez."

#. We watch your ledgers the way a rival merchant watches a loaded cart.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/envy/1"
msgstr "Nous regardons vos registres comme un marchand rival regarde une charrette chargée."

#. Whatever you raise, we shall raise beside it. That is simply how it must be.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/envy/2"
msgstr "Ce que vous élèverez, nous l'élèverons à côté. Ainsi va le monde, et il n'y a rien à y faire."

#. We shall not be dragged through your quarrels. Our own fields interest us more than your treaties.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/isolationist/0"
msgstr "On ne nous traînera pas dans vos querelles. Nos champs nous intéressent plus que vos traités."

#. An alliance is a rope with two ends, and we prefer our hands free.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/isolationist/1"
msgstr "Une alliance est une corde à deux bouts, et nous préférons avoir les mains libres."

#. Your envoy will find our harbour open and our court busy with its own accounts.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/isolationist/2"
msgstr "Votre envoyé trouvera notre port ouvert et notre cour occupée de ses propres comptes."

#. Every war ends. We would rather it ended before the terms cost us both a province.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/peacemaker/0"
msgstr "Toute guerre finit. Nous préférerions qu'elle finît avant que ses conditions ne nous coûtent à tous deux une province."

#. Our squadrons sail to see a fight stopped, not to start one.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/peacemaker/1"
msgstr "Nos escadres appareillent pour faire cesser une querelle, non pour en allumer une."

#. When the next crown is carved up, we intend to be the hand on the knife's wrist.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/peacemaker/2"
msgstr "Quand la prochaine couronne sera partagée, nous entendons être la main sur le poignet du couteau."

#. Your colleges publish; ours listen. It is cheaper than teaching our own scholars.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/tech_thief/0"
msgstr "Vos collèges publient ; les nôtres écoutent. Cela coûte moins que d'instruire nos propres savants."

#. A study kept secret is worth less than one our agents can read. You should consider that.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/tech_thief/1"
msgstr "Une étude tenue secrète vaut moins qu'une autre que nos agents peuvent lire. Vous devriez y songer."

#. Our gentlemen of letters are patient men. They read the papers your court leaves out.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/tech_thief/2"
msgstr "Nos gens de lettres sont des hommes patients. Ils lisent les papiers que votre cour laisse traîner."

#. There is a crown in these waters with a thin wall and a fat treasury. We are patient, not idle.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/warmonger/0"
msgstr "Il est en ces eaux une couronne à la muraille mince et au trésor gras. Nous sommes patients, non oisifs."

#. Our regiments drill while your merchants count. One of those numbers will matter more.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/warmonger/1"
msgstr "Nos régiments s'exercent pendant que vos marchands comptent. L'un de ces nombres pèsera davantage."

#. A neighbour's weakness is a standing invitation. We have never been good at refusing one.
msgid "DialoguePoint/agenda/warmonger/2"
msgstr "La faiblesse d'un voisin est une invite permanente. Nous n'avons jamais su en refuser une."

#. The treaty served its season. It serves no longer.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_them/0"
msgstr "Le traité a fait sa saison. Il ne la fera plus."

#. We renounce the alliance; our ships sail where we bid them.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_them/1"
msgstr "Nous renonçons à l'alliance ; nos vaisseaux vont où nous l'ordonnons."

#. Do not look for our squadrons. You will not find them beside you.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_them/2"
msgstr "Ne cherchez plus nos escadres. Vous ne les trouverez point à vos côtés."

#. You break your word before witnesses. We shall remember it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_you/0"
msgstr "Vous rompez votre parole devant témoins. Nous nous en souviendrons."

#. Our clerks have written your name beside this day.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_you/1"
msgstr "Nos clercs ont inscrit votre nom en regard de ce jour."

#. So a crown keeps faith. Good to know before the next treaty.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_broken_by_you/2"
msgstr "Voilà donc comme une couronne garde la foi. Bon à savoir avant le prochain traité."

#. Your enemies are ours now, and ours are yours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_formed/0"
msgstr "Vos ennemis sont nôtres désormais, et les nôtres sont vôtres."

#. Let the treaty be read aloud in both our harbours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_formed/1"
msgstr "Que le traité soit lu à haute voix dans nos deux ports."

#. We stand with you, so long as the terms stand.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/alliance_formed/2"
msgstr "Nous demeurons avec vous, tant que les conditions tiendront."

#. Our regiments are yours in this quarrel.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_joined/0"
msgstr "Nos régiments sont vôtres en cette querelle."

#. The treaty speaks plainly, and so do we. We march.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_joined/1"
msgstr "Le traité parle clair, et nous aussi. Nous marchons."

#. Consider the aggressor answered.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_joined/2"
msgstr "Tenez l'agresseur pour répondu."

#. The treaty did not bind us to this ruin. Our regiments stay home.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_refused/0"
msgstr "Le traité ne nous liait point à cette ruine. Nos régiments restent au pays."

#. We have weighed this war. You will fight it without us.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_refused/1"
msgstr "Nous avons pesé cette guerre. Vous la ferez sans nous."

#. Do not mistake our refusal for friendship to the other side.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/call_to_arms_refused/2"
msgstr "Ne prenez pas notre refus pour amitié envers l'autre parti."

#. We had heard of your crown. Now we shall learn what it is worth.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/first_contact/0"
msgstr "Nous avions ouï parler de votre couronne. Nous verrons maintenant ce qu'elle vaut."

#. Send word who you are, that our clerks may enter it properly.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/first_contact/1"
msgstr "Mandez-nous qui vous êtes, afin que nos clercs l'inscrivent comme il se doit."

#. A new flag in these waters. {other}, is it? We shall watch where it sails.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/first_contact/2"
msgstr "Un pavillon nouveau dans ces eaux. {other}, n'est-ce pas ? Nous verrons où il fait voile."

#. We will not stand by while a crown is carved up.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_joined/0"
msgstr "Nous ne resterons pas cois tandis qu'on dépèce une couronne."

#. Our squadrons sail. The aggressor had better mind its charts.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_joined/1"
msgstr "Nos escadres appareillent. Que l'agresseur prenne garde à ses cartes."

#. The embassy stood for this. We answer it now.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_joined/2"
msgstr "Notre ambassade s'y était engagée. Nous y répondons aujourd'hui."

#. This war is an outrage, and our court says so plainly.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_protested/0"
msgstr "Cette guerre est une horreur, et notre cour le dit tout net."

#. We protest this aggression in every court that will hear us.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_protested/1"
msgstr "Nous protestons contre cette agression en toute cour qui nous voudra ouïr."

#. There will be a reckoning for this, though not today with guns.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_protested/2"
msgstr "Il y aura compte à rendre, encore que ce ne soit pas aujourd'hui par les canons."

#. Our embassy is closed. What follows is not our affair.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_stood_aside/0"
msgstr "Notre ambassade est close. Ce qui suit n'est point notre affaire."

#. We have taken the papers home. The war is yours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_stood_aside/1"
msgstr "Nous avons rapporté nos papiers. La guerre est vôtre."

#. We choose our quarrels. This is not one of them.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/intervention_stood_aside/2"
msgstr "Nous choisissons nos querelles. Celle-ci n'en est pas."

#. Your envoy is welcome. Our clerks will find him a chair.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_accepted/0"
msgstr "Votre envoyé est le bienvenu. Nos clercs lui trouveront un siège."

#. We accept. Let it be entered in the book of treaties.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_accepted/1"
msgstr "Nous acceptons. Qu'on l'inscrive au livre des traités."

#. A small step, and a useful one. Come, let us sign.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_accepted/2"
msgstr "Un petit pas, et qui sert. Allons, signons."

#. Our envoy shall keep your court, and your merchants our ports.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_granted/0"
msgstr "Notre envoyé tiendra votre cour, et vos marchands nos ports."

#. It is agreed. Let the papers be sealed and the wine poured.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_granted/1"
msgstr "C'est convenu. Qu'on scelle les papiers et qu'on verse le vin."

#. We receive your envoy kindly, and expect the courtesy returned.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_granted/2"
msgstr "Nous recevons votre envoyé de bon cœur, et comptons qu'on nous rende la courtoisie."

#. The terms do not suit us. Keep your envoy at home.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_refused/0"
msgstr "Ces conditions ne nous agréent point. Gardez votre envoyé chez vous."

#. A consul from your court would find little to do here.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_refused/1"
msgstr "Un consul de votre cour trouverait peu à faire céans."

#. No. We need nothing from you badly enough to grant this.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_refused/2"
msgstr "Non. Rien de ce qu'il nous faut ne vaut de vous l'accorder."

#. Very well. We shall not ask twice.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_withdrawn/0"
msgstr "Fort bien. Nous ne demanderons pas deux fois."

#. Your refusal is entered in the ledger, and not in your favour.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_withdrawn/1"
msgstr "Votre refus est porté au registre, et non à votre avantage."

#. Then we keep our envoy, and our money, at home.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/overture_withdrawn/2"
msgstr "Alors nous gardons notre envoyé, et notre argent, chez nous."

#. Enough blood has gone to the fishes. The war is done.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/peace_made/0"
msgstr "Assez de sang est allé aux poissons. La guerre est faite."

#. The treaty is signed. Let no captain test the ink.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/peace_made/1"
msgstr "Le traité est signé. Que nul capitaine n'éprouve l'encre."

#. We shall have peace, and watch you the closer for it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/peace_made/2"
msgstr "Nous aurons la paix, et vous observerons d'autant plus près."

#. It is agreed. Our clerks will draw it up before the day is out.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_accepted/0"
msgstr "C'est convenu. Nos clercs le dresseront avant la fin du jour."

#. You have dealt with us fairly. We shall remember it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_accepted/1"
msgstr "Vous avez traité avec nous loyalement. Nous nous en souviendrons."

#. Then let it be finished, and let both fleets know it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_accepted/2"
msgstr "Qu'on en finisse, et que les deux flottes le sachent."

#. Very well. The offer is withdrawn.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_refused/0"
msgstr "Fort bien. L'offre est retirée."

#. We had expected better of your court. So be it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_refused/1"
msgstr "Nous attendions mieux de votre cour. Ainsi soit-il."

#. The offer dies here. Do not come asking after it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/proposal_refused/2"
msgstr "L'offre expire ici. Ne revenez pas la réclamer."

#. You have had our patience. Now you shall have our broadsides.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_them/0"
msgstr "Vous avez eu notre patience. Vous aurez maintenant nos bordées."

#. Our guns are laid, our letters are finished, and our patience is spent.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_them/1"
msgstr "Nos canons sont pointés, nos lettres sont écrites, et notre patience épuisée."

#. Let the sea judge between our crowns, since the court could not.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_them/2"
msgstr "Que la mer juge entre nos couronnes, puisque la cour n'a su le faire."

#. So be it. Every sail you take shall be answered for at the peace.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_you/0"
msgstr "Ainsi soit-il. Chaque voile prise vous sera comptée à la paix."

#. You strike first. We shall be the last to strike.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_you/1"
msgstr "Vous frappez le premier. Nous serons les derniers à frapper."

#. Our harbours are shut to your flag, and our cruisers are not idle.
msgid "DialoguePoint/diplomatic/war_declared_by_you/2"
msgstr "Nos ports sont clos à votre pavillon, et nos frégates ne chôment point."

#. Your seat lies under our guns. Open the gates and spare the houses.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/capital_threatened/0"
msgstr "Votre siège est sous nos canons. Ouvrez les portes et épargnez les maisons."

#. We stand before your palace, and the question left is only how long.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/capital_threatened/1"
msgstr "Nous sommes devant votre palais, et la seule question qui reste est : combien de temps."

#. The town is ours to take when we choose it. Sleep on that.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/capital_threatened/2"
msgstr "La ville est à nous quand il nous plaira. Dormez là-dessus."

#. Your flag is over our land. We were not asked, only told.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/colony_founded/0"
msgstr "Votre pavillon flotte sur notre terre. On ne nous a pas demandé, on nous a dit."

#. You have bought our elders and our ground in the same handshake.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/colony_founded/1"
msgstr "Vous avez acheté nos anciens et notre sol d'une seule poignée de main."

#. The musket and the chapel came off the same ship. We carry both now.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/colony_founded/2"
msgstr "Le mousquet et la chapelle sont venus du même navire. Nous portons l'un et l'autre à présent."

#. Our line broke on yours. The court has read every name aloud.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_lost/0"
msgstr "Notre ligne s'est rompue sur la vôtre. La cour a lu chaque nom à haute voix."

#. We shall not dress it: the field was yours, and the colours with it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_lost/1"
msgstr "Nous ne farderons rien : le champ fut vôtre, et les couleurs avec lui."

#. Our colours are in your hands. Do not think the war is in them.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_lost/2"
msgstr "Nos couleurs sont en vos mains. Ne croyez pas que la guerre y soit."

#. Our line broke theirs in the open. The prisoners are already counting themselves.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_won/0"
msgstr "Notre ligne a rompu la leur en rase campagne. Les prisonniers se comptent déjà."

#. You brought your regiments into the open, and the open kept ours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_won/1"
msgstr "Vous avez mené vos régiments en plein champ, et le plein champ a gardé les nôtres."

#. The field is ours. We shall bury theirs and thank the ground for it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/field_won/2"
msgstr "Le champ est nôtre. Nous enterrerons les leurs et remercierons la terre."

#. Our squadron went down with the sun. The sea keeps what it takes.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_lost/0"
msgstr "Notre escadre a sombré avec le soleil. La mer garde ce qu'elle prend."

#. The water is yours. Our captains will be asked hard questions.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_lost/1"
msgstr "L'eau est vôtre. On fera à nos capitaines de dures questions."

#. We lost the station and the hulls with it. That is the whole of the news.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_lost/2"
msgstr "Nous avons perdu la station, et les coques avec elle. Voilà toute la nouvelle."

#. Our broadsides settled it. The water is ours, and the wreckage with it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_won/0"
msgstr "Nos bordées en ont décidé. L'eau est nôtre, et les débris avec elle."

#. Your squadron went down with the sun. We counted the masts from the shore.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_won/1"
msgstr "Votre escadre a sombré avec le soleil. Nous avons compté les mâts du rivage."

#. The sea answered for us. Send no more sail where ours keeps station.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/sea_won/2"
msgstr "La mer a répondu pour nous. N'envoyez plus de voiles où les nôtres tiennent leur poste."

#. The walls held. Your batteries bought nothing but smoke and patience.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_held/0"
msgstr "Les murailles ont tenu. Vos batteries n'ont acheté que de la fumée et de la patience."

#. You broke on our ramparts. The guns are still ours, and so is the town.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_held/1"
msgstr "Vous vous êtes brisé sur nos remparts. Les canons sont encore à nous, et la ville aussi."

#. Our stones outlasted your train. Come again when you have more of it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_held/2"
msgstr "Nos pierres ont plus duré que votre artillerie. Revenez quand vous en aurez davantage."

#. Our guns fell silent before the wall did. The siege is raised.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_lost/0"
msgstr "Nos canons se sont tus avant la muraille. Le siège est levé."

#. We shall not spend another train on those stones this year.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_lost/1"
msgstr "Nous ne dépenserons pas une autre artillerie sur ces pierres cette année."

#. The wall stood and our batteries did not. The court will hear of it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_lost/2"
msgstr "La muraille a tenu et nos batteries non. La cour en sera informée."

#. The breach is yours and the town with it. We shall want it back.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_taken/0"
msgstr "La brèche est vôtre, et la ville avec elle. Nous la voudrons retrouver."

#. Our walls failed us. The court is being told so this very hour.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_taken/1"
msgstr "Nos murailles nous ont trahis. On le mande à la cour à cette heure même."

#. You have the town. The stones remember who raised them.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_taken/2"
msgstr "La ville est à vous. Les pierres se souviennent qui les a élevées."

#. The breach is ours and the town with it. Our batteries did the talking.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_won/0"
msgstr "La brèche est nôtre, et la ville avec elle. Ce sont nos batteries qui ont parlé."

#. Your walls came down in the end. We shall hold them better than you did.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_won/1"
msgstr "Vos murailles sont enfin tombées. Nous les tiendrons mieux que vous."

#. The garrison answered our last summons with a flag. The town is ours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/siege_won/2"
msgstr "La garnison a répondu à notre dernière sommation par un drapeau. La ville est nôtre."

#. Your scholars publish while ours still argue. We have taken note of it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/tech_studied/0"
msgstr "Vos savants publient tandis que les nôtres disputent encore. Nous en avons pris note."

#. So the crown has learned something new. Our admirals will want to hear it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/tech_studied/1"
msgstr "La couronne a donc appris chose nouvelle. Nos amiraux voudront l'entendre."

#. Every study your court finishes makes our own colleges quieter. Go carefully.
msgid "DialoguePoint/event/tech_studied/2"
msgstr "Chaque étude que votre cour achève rend nos collèges plus silencieux. Prenez garde."

#. An alliance, then. Two crowns hold a sea better than one.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_alliance/0"
msgstr "Une alliance, donc. Deux couronnes tiennent mieux une mer qu'une seule."

#. Our courts are close enough in mind. Shall we put it in ink?
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_alliance/1"
msgstr "Nos cours s'accordent assez. La mettrons-nous par écrit ?"

#. Sign with us, and neither of us faces the next war alone.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_alliance/2"
msgstr "Signez avec nous, et nul de nous n'affrontera seul la prochaine guerre."

#. A consul at your court and your merchants at our quay. Shall we?
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_overture/0"
msgstr "Un consul en votre cour et vos marchands sur notre quai. Est-ce dit ?"

#. We propose an arrangement of mutual use. The papers are ready.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_overture/1"
msgstr "Nous proposons un arrangement de profit commun. Les papiers sont prêts."

#. Small treaties keep the peace. Come, agree to one.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_overture/2"
msgstr "Les petits traités gardent la paix. Allons, consentez-y."

#. Let the guns fall silent. We offer a white peace.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_peace/0"
msgstr "Que les canons se taisent. Nous offrons une paix blanche."

#. We have both lost enough ships to this war. Shall we stop?
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_peace/1"
msgstr "Nous avons tous deux perdu assez de vaisseaux dans cette guerre. Cessons-nous ?"

#. Our terms are a white peace, no more and no less. Answer it.
msgid "DialoguePoint/negotiation/proposal_peace/2"
msgstr "Nos conditions sont une paix blanche, rien de plus ni de moins. Répondez-y."

#. Your court is always welcome here, and your squadrons beside ours.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_alliance/0"
msgstr "Votre cour est toujours bienvenue céans, et vos escadres à côté des nôtres."

#. The alliance holds. Long may it suit us both.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_alliance/1"
msgstr "L'alliance tient. Puissent nos deux cours s'en trouver bien longtemps."

#. We have little to say to your court.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_cold/0"
msgstr "Nous avons peu à dire à votre cour."

#. Our clerks record your name, and nothing warmer.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_cold/1"
msgstr "Nos clercs y inscrivent votre nom, et rien de plus chaleureux."

#. You will always find a friend of our court in this harbour.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_friendly/0"
msgstr "Vous trouverez toujours un ami de notre cour en ce port."

#. Our doors are open to your envoy, at any hour.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_friendly/1"
msgstr "Nos portes sont ouvertes à votre envoyé, à toute heure."

#. Our clerks record your name; nothing more today.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_neutral/0"
msgstr "Nos clercs inscrivent votre nom ; rien de plus aujourd'hui."

#. The court is civil, and no more than civil.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_neutral/1"
msgstr "La cour est civile, et rien que civile."

#. The war stands. We shall speak again when one of us tires.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_war/0"
msgstr "La guerre tient. Nous reparlerons quand l'un de nous s'en lassera."

#. Our courts have nothing to add to the guns.
msgid "DialoguePoint/reactive/standing_war/1"
msgstr "Nos cours n'ont rien à ajouter aux canons."

